"""Sample documents so the app can be demoed instantly without an upload."""

DEMO_LEASE = """RESIDENTIAL LEASE AGREEMENT

This Lease Agreement ("Agreement") is entered into between Meridian Housing LLC ("Landlord") and the undersigned tenant ("Tenant") for the property located at 14 Willow Court, Unit 3B.

1. Term. This Agreement begins on the Commencement Date and continues for a fixed term of 12 months. Upon expiration, this Agreement shall automatically renew for successive 12-month terms unless either party provides written notice of non-renewal at least 60 days before the end of the then-current term.

2. Rent. Tenant shall pay monthly rent of $1,850, due on the 1st of each month. Any payment received after the 5th of the month shall incur a late fee of $75 plus $10 per additional day of delay.

3. Security Deposit. Tenant shall pay a refundable security deposit of $1,850 prior to move-in. The deposit may be applied to unpaid rent, damages beyond normal wear and tear, or cleaning costs, and the remaining balance will be returned within 30 days of move-out.

4. Early Termination. Should Tenant terminate this Agreement prior to the end of the fixed term for any reason other than those enumerated under applicable law, Tenant shall be liable for an early termination fee equal to two (2) months' rent, in addition to rent owed through the date of termination.

5. Maintenance and Repairs. Tenant shall promptly notify Landlord of any needed repairs. Landlord shall be responsible for structural repairs and major systems (plumbing, electrical, HVAC). Tenant is responsible for damage caused by Tenant's negligence or misuse.

6. Use of Premises. The premises shall be used solely as a private residence. Tenant shall not sublet the unit, in whole or in part, without prior written consent of Landlord, which consent shall not be unreasonably withheld.

7. Pets. No pets are permitted on the premises without prior written approval from Landlord and payment of a non-refundable pet fee of $300 per approved pet.

8. Confidentiality of Tenant Records. Landlord shall not disclose Tenant's personal or financial information to third parties except as required by law or for legitimate business purposes such as credit reporting.

9. Notice of Termination. Either party seeking to terminate this Agreement at the end of a term must provide written notice no less than 60 days prior to the term's expiration date, delivered by certified mail or verified email.

10. Non-Compete for Subletting Platforms. Tenant agrees not to list the unit, or any portion thereof, on any short-term rental or hospitality platform for the duration of this Agreement.

11. Dispute Resolution. Any dispute arising under this Agreement shall first be submitted to non-binding mediation. If mediation fails to resolve the dispute within 30 days, either party may pursue binding arbitration in accordance with the rules of the American Arbitration Association. Tenant waives the right to a jury trial for disputes arising under this Agreement.

12. Rent Increases. Landlord reserves the right to increase rent upon renewal by an amount to be determined at Landlord's discretion, subject to applicable local rent control ordinances, with notice provided at least 45 days before the renewal date.

13. Governing Law. This Agreement shall be governed by the laws of the state in which the premises are located."""

